      "Authorized public source/configuration artifacts and effective defaults for baseline-din, r0001-ordinary_din and all four round-3 arms; compare embedding/scorer algebra, parameter construction and initialization order, RNG consumption, masks, dtype and checkpoint-selection logic. Receipt claims and equal parameter counts alone do not establish equivalence. Ancestor sources are not exposed in this workspace.",
      "Host-provided reproducibility metadata: actual seed/RNG settings, deterministic-kernel policy, software/device versions, data order, training and validation histories, selected epoch, and checkpoint identities. If permitted, same-input initial/final logits or gradients could localize drift. Do not inspect credentials or runtime internals or assume these diagnostics are available.",
      "Explicit later-phase host interface for registered-source execution and paired seeds 43/44. The active protocol declares train_seed=42; do not silently edit it. Clarify whether one bounded, known-state seed-42 ordinary bridge rerun is admissible and whether all four registered arms differ solely in the intended factors before repeating them.",
      "Complete paired-seed factorial receipts, including failures and costs, for ordinary, cross-removal, context-removal and joint arms. Report joint-minus-ordinary, joint-minus-cross, both factor simple effects and their interaction for AUC and Logloss. Existing receipts are single-seed; no confidence interval or independent-user significance can be inferred from exposure counts.",
      "If robustness warrants a later mechanism experiment, primary-source methods and executable details for same-field versus cross-field target-history interactions and scale-controlled replacement controls. Inspect DIN section 4.3 and nearest field-aware interaction work directly before any priority claim; retrieved agent-r0003 supplies source locators but is secondary evidence. Novelty remains unverified. No industry card currently resolves the bridge or semantic-versus-scale uncertainty, so no card is requested by lexical association.",
      "Authorized product-block norm, score-dispersion, attention-entropy and same-checkpoint diagnostics sufficient to distinguish scale changes from semantic pairing, with a prospective scale/term-count-matched replacement design, predictions and falsifiers recorded before execution. Current candidate-authored first-512 diagnostics establish numerical activity only and cannot establish semantic relevance or whole-population benefit.",
